A||||5||Scott2M4||1995 Fiero Concepts - I was bored in study hall ...||||1||
Z||000000||Scott2M4||01-13-2000||07:26 AM||||I guess I had an interest in the Pontiac Fiero earlier than 11/02/99.  While cleaning out my closet last night, I found these three drawings I did back in 1995.  Someone on the forum recently mentioned their introduction into automotive design making the placement of these drawings on the forum seem appropriate.  Maybe that person can take these back and get our car going again!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/95Fiero1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/95Fiero2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/95Fiero3.jpg"> <P>What do you all think?  Do you like any of them?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||01-13-2000||10:09 AM||||I like all of them. But I think the middle one is my favorite. Probly just because of the wing. If it didn't have the wing, I'd go for the first one. Wings on regular Fieros look best on the GT. I like the notchback better without them.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||01-13-2000||11:28 AM||||Very, very nice! I think my favorite is the last one because it still has some typical Fiero lines in it (particularly the nose and back).||||reg||14
Z||000003||Phil||01-13-2000||01:48 PM||||Nice designs BUT I think one of the attractions of the the Fiero was/is that it didn't/doesn't  look like anything else. To me all the new designs today look very similar.The same for all the various dash kits, the Fiero was unique and all of the kits tend to resemble any new car of today. I'm wearing my asbestos suit so have at it guys||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||01-13-2000||07:20 PM||||2m4,<P>Well done!  Especially since the drawings are congruent with current designs yet are 5 years old.  I personally prefer the last one.  It has more of a european look to it.  The first one has a nice side air induction though.  The middle has a slight resemblance with a Mitsu eclipse.  Well now that you have my approval, you may start on that body kit. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-14-2000||04:20 AM||||Here's what you do.  Take the nose, mirrors and wing off of the middle one and put them on the top pic.  The roof line on the bottom one needs to be there too.  And take the Ford wheels off the top and replace them with something a little more exotic.  There you have it.  My future car.  <B> Now </B> you may proceed.  Can we assume that the motor (big 6, please) will be in the rear?||||reg||1
